description.narrative:
The objective of the Sida/AFD co-guarantee to Equity BCDC in DRC is to facilitate the access to finance for Micro Small Medium Enterprises (MSMEs), to expand access to financing for high impact sectors such as health, education and renewable energy. MSMEs in these sectors often lack collateral and necessary credit history to expand their activities.

The intervention is expected to contribute to increasing the share of competitive MSMEs in the economy, the development of the overall private sector, employment and economic growth and access to renewable energy, education and health, which in turn will help improve livelihoods in the DRC.

The desired achievements of the program are to:

1. Increase lending for MSMEs targeting health, education and renewable energy sectors, by sharing risks with AFD/Proparco and Equity BCDC and mobilizing private capital;

2. Increased lending to women and youth owned MSMEs;

3. Enable the Bank to improve their internal capacity to serve MSMEs through skills enhancement and provide technical assistance to MSMEs, to support MSMEs to improve their internal capacity in financial management and their growth during and after financing; 

4. Contribute to more favourable lending requirements (longer tenors for example) for MSMEs in the underserved sectors in the DRC;

5. Create a transparent reporting through the monitoring and follow up of the development results.

The expected impact of the program is to significantly and sustainably increase the financing of MSMEs, mainly in the health, education and renewable energy sectors and an increased economic growth and improved living conditions for people in the DRC.
